module Numerics

# The amount of a shift and the index of a subscript may be an `Integer`: the builder turns it into the type the
# routine takes with these (the fixed-width integers have theirs in Core).

### This value as an index: the same count as a `U64`, or `U64_MAX` when it is larger.
### :returns: The count as a `U64`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when this value is below 0.
routine Integer.to_index!() -> U64
    if me.neg
        throw NumericDomainError(description: f"{me} is below 0, and an index counts from 0")
    if me > U64_MAX.to[Integer]()
        return U64_MAX
    return me.to[U64]()

### This value as a shift amount: the same count as a `U32`, or `U32_MAX` when it is larger.
### :returns: The count as a `U32`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when this value is below 0.
routine Integer.to_shift_amount!() -> U32
    if me.neg
        throw NumericDomainError(description: f"{me} is below 0, and a shift amount counts from 0")
    if me > U32_MAX.to[Integer]()
        return U32_MAX
    return me.to[U32]()

# A Suflae subscript or shift takes an `Integer` count: a fixed-width one becomes an `Integer` with these.

### This value as an `Integer` count (an index or a shift amount), the same number.
### :returns: The value as an `Integer`.
routine S8.to_integer_count() -> Integer
    return me.to[Integer]()

### This value as an `Integer` count (an index or a shift amount), the same number.
### :returns: The value as an `Integer`.
routine S16.to_integer_count() -> Integer
    return me.to[Integer]()

